.policy "complexity-cyclomatic-vue" revision 2
.description "Keep the functions of a Vue component's scripts at cyclomatic complexity 6 or below, counting each if, loop, catch, switch, ternary and && or ||; branch-heavy functions are hard to follow and test."
.language vue
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.vue"
.scope exclude "**/node_modules/**", "**/dist/**", "**/build/**", "**/out/**", "**/.nuxt/**", "**/.output/**"
.scope exclude "**/coverage/**", "**/generated/**", "**/__generated__/**", "**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*", "**/__tests__/**"

#include "complexity/ecma.rr"
#include "vue/component.rr"
//   cc_report(f, msg)   function f has cyclomatic complexity over 6 (lizard's decision points; nested ones apart)
//   vscript(p, setup)   p is the program of a <script> block (setup "true" for <script setup>)

// The complexity pack's ceiling for the functions of a component's <script> and <script setup> blocks, counted as
// the TypeScript and JavaScript rules count them. The template's expressions and directives (v-if, v-for,
// @click="() => …") run in no function of the scripts, so they are never scored:
//   <script setup> function grade(s) { if … else if (a && b) … for … while … switch (s) { case 1: … } } </script>
//   -> `grade` has cyclomatic complexity 7, over the ceiling of 6.
.violation complexity(at: node, msg: symbol) code "CYCLOMATIC_COMPLEXITY" "{msg}"
complexity(f, msg) :- cc_report(f, msg), vscript(p, _), within(f, p).
